- **Developer artifacts in the product UI.**
  - Design System is in the main nav.
  - Page titles show literal backticks.
  - Raw IDs are visible (`ach-k8s-ingest`).
  - Copy uses implementation words (catalog, descriptor, deterministic, ResumeVersion, "Atomic").
  - A "Preview Import Review Flow" button is still present.
  - There are three separate entry points to demo mode.
- **Competing actions.**
  - Applications shows two filled-blue buttons and a four-action header.
  - Each version card has three buttons.
  - Export PDF appears twice on the Review step.
  - Save version appears twice on an empty timeline.
  - The selected provider in Settings looks like a primary button.
- **Studio.**
  - Four tall stepper cards sit above the work area.
  - Tailor stacks three tall cards (Voice dial, Live sample, Summary) before the first bullet.
  - The dial duplicates the five detent cards, is clipped at the bottom, and some detent text truncates ("Formal leadershi…"); one label overflows its card ("Plain-spoken").
  - The preview jumps from the right side (Tailor) to the left side (Review).
  - Back and Next sit at the top while the work ends at the bottom.
- **Review.** Gauges and long explanations are squeezed into a ~500px column, and the score breakdown is a monospace text table.
- **Bank.** A 180px dropzone is permanent, every field of every role and achievement is an open input, and delete icons are everywhere.
- **Settings.** The demo provider exposes meaningless "profile" fields. Four data buttons carry equal weight, including a filled red Wipe. The theme is set in two places.
- **Typography and density.**
  - Monospace is used for dates, scores, labels, URLs and taglines.
  - Secondary text is 11 to 12px, too small at desk distance.
  - Native `<select>` elements clash with the design system.
