## 5. Cover Letter feature

### 5.1 Concept
Each application has two documents: **Resume** and **Cover letter**. They share the Job analysis, the Bank, the Voice control, the template family, and the versions model. A letter is built from the same truthful sources as the resume.

### 5.2 Write step (work panel)
1. **Setup** (a compact card, collapsible after the first generation):
   - Recipient (optional, defaults to "Hiring Team").
   - Length: Short (150–220 words) / Standard (250–350) / Detailed (350–450).
   - **Proof points:** up to 3 Bank achievements as chips. Pre-selected from the resume's chosen bullets, ranked by relevance to the top requirements, and changeable.
   - "Why this company" (optional): a text area for the user's **own words**. Show a hint: "Add a sentence on why you want this company to make the letter stand out."
   - The shared Voice control. The letter's default is one detent more human than the resume's default.
2. **Generate** (sparkle icon, AI actions only). The letter streams into **blocks**: Greeting, Opening, Body 1, Body 2 (optional), Why this company (only if the user supplied notes, or if the JD itself contains a mission statement to reference), Closing, Sign-off.
3. Each block is editable inline, with regenerate, lock, and a "From: …" chip showing its source Bank achievements.

### 5.3 Grounding rules (non-negotiable)
Letter facts may come only from (a) the Bank, (b) the job description text, and (c) the user's "why this company" notes. Never invent facts about the company, its products, or the hiring manager. Run the grounding validator on every generation. Numbers, tools, and employers that don't trace to those sources get the "Unverified" badge.

### 5.4 Review step for letters
- **Gauges area:** **Job match** (reused requirement coverage) and **Letter check** ("5 of 6 checks passed"). There is no ATS gauge for letters.
- **Letter check items** (deterministic): length within the chosen band; mentions the role title and company; covers at least 3 of the top requirements; at least 2 specific proof points (when the Bank has metrics); no cliché openers or phrases ("I am writing to express my interest", "I am excited to apply", "passionate", "great fit"); no unverified claims. Also report paragraph count (3 to 5) and the share of sentences starting with "I" (warn above 50%).
- Include the Machine-made feel meter.
- **Preview:** one-page letter in the same template as the resume (header, date, recipient, salutation, body, sign-off) with a live word count. Warn on overflow.
- **Export:** same split button: PDF (default), Markdown, Plain text, Copy as text. The PDF is real text and goes through the same round-trip check.

### 5.5 Persistence and history
Letters use the same version model (kind = `coverLetter`), the Applications detail tab, compare, and duplicate. "Duplicate application" offers to duplicate the letter too, with a reminder to re-check company-specific sentences.

## 6. Design-system changes
- **Scale:** set the root size with utilities on `<html>` (15px base, 16px at ≥1920px, 18px at ≥2560px). All sizes are in rem, so the UI scales as a whole. No text below 13px at base.
- **Type roles:** Title (serif display, page titles and resume name only), Section (sans 600), Body 15, Caption 13, Numeric (sans with tabular figures). **Monospace is reserved for code, URLs and file paths.** Scores, dates and counts use sans with tabular numerals.
- **Selected vs primary:** the filled accent is only for the single primary action on a screen. Selected toggles, radio-cards and segments use an accent-subtle background, accent border and a check.
- **Icons:** one set (lucide). **Sparkles only mean "AI action."** Icon-only buttons need a tooltip and `aria-label`.
- **Replace every native `<select>`** with the Select primitive. Use SegmentedControl for small fixed choices.
- **Density:** list rows at least 56px; interactive targets at least 36px (primary at least 40px); at least 16px between destructive and primary controls; fewer borders (rely on surface contrast).
- **Layout tokens:** sidebar 232px or 72px; page content max width 1480px (non-Studio); Studio work panel 560 to 760px; gutters 24px (32px at ≥1920px); prose max 70ch.
- **New or changed components:** SidebarNav, StatusPill, PageHeader, DocumentSwitch, CompactStepper, SegmentedControl, SplitButton, Select, Drawer, ConfirmDialog (with typed-confirm variant), Toast with Undo, Disclosure, EmptyState, GettingStartedCard, VoiceControl (compact dial), BulletRow, ScoreChip, Gauge, ExplanationTooltip, LetterBlock, CommandPalette, Code. Each is documented with states on `/design-system`.

## 7. Copy rules
Sentence case. Buttons are verbs. Subtitles are one line. No implementation words in visible text: catalog, descriptor, schema, deterministic, port, ID, ResumeVersion, "atomic". Add a small unit test that scans the web adapter's string literals for a banned-terms list (with an allow-list for the design-system page).

| Before | After |
|---|---|
| Cevin Studio, Apps, Bank, Style, LLM Connection | Cevin; Applications, Experience Bank, Settings |
| First-Run Guide / Demo Mode | Getting started (checklist); Load demo data (Settings) |
| Atomic Achievements | Achievements |
| Action / Result / Verified Metric | What you did / What changed / Metric |
| Supported formats from catalog: … | Drop a PDF, Markdown or text file |
| Locality: Local Machine Only | Runs on your computer |
| Deterministic Profile, Embedding Profile | (removed in demo mode); Advanced > Embedding model |
| Generated dynamically from … descriptors | (removed) |
| Exporting automatically saves an immutable ResumeVersion | Exporting also saves this as a new version |
| Sounds machine-made (heuristic): 15/100 | Machine-made feel: Low (tooltip: a style estimate, not an AI detector) |
| Deterministic code evaluation (keywords 45%…) | Tooltip "How this is calculated" with plain bullets |
| Load into Studio | Open this version |

## 8. Defects to fix (with unit tests)
1. **Bullet assembly:** join action and result with a comma or an em dash and **never** produce ". lowercase". Append the Metric only if its numeric tokens are not already in the text. Examples that must pass: (a) a result containing "38%" and "1.4M events/sec" plus a metric of the same values produces no repeated clause; (b) never output "…layer. dropping…" or "…by 38%: 38% egress…". Keep punctuation consistent (all bullets end the same way).
2. **Contact block:** two deliberate lines (email, phone, location; then links). Separators only between items, never at a line end. Links are shown without "https://", in the body font, with no "GitHub:"-style labels.
3. **Resume typography:** dates and URLs in the body font with tabular numerals. Dates right-aligned on the role line when they fit.
4. Voice dial clipping, truncated detent text, and overflowing labels (all fixed by the compact VoiceControl).
5. Remove duplicate actions: navigation, Export PDF, Save version, demo-mode entry points, theme toggle.
6. Literal backticks in headings; filled-blue misuse on Settings and Applications.

## 9. Architecture impact (stay hexagonal)
- **Domain:**
  - Add `DocumentKind = "resume" | "coverLetter"`.
  - Add `CoverLetter { blocks[{ type, text, sourceIds, locked }], recipient, length, voice }` and the `CoverLetterDocument` view model with a mapper `toCoverLetterDocument`.
  - Add letter analysis rules (word bands, opener and cliché list, requirement coverage, "I"-start ratio) and a bullet assembler module.
  - Reuse the voice mapping, AI-ism linter and grounding validator.
- **Ports and use cases:**
  - Generalize `ResumeExporter` into `DocumentExporter` with `supports: DocumentKind[]`, taking `ExportableDocument = ResumeDocument | CoverLetterDocument`. PDF, Markdown and Text declare both kinds. Registries and the "one adapter plus one registry line" rule are unchanged.
  - Generalize `ExportResume` into `ExportDocument`, `SaveResumeVersion` into `SaveDocumentVersion(kind)`, and `ListExportFormats(kind)`.
  - New inbound use cases: `GenerateCoverLetter`, `RewriteLetterBlock`, `ScoreCoverLetter`, `GetConnectionStatus`.
  - Templates become `DocumentTemplate`, rendering both kinds.
- **Storage:** `Application.documents` holds `{ resume, coverLetter }`, each with a working draft. `ResumeVersion` becomes `DocumentVersion { kind, … }`. Ship a Dexie migration that converts existing versions to `kind = "resume"`, with a test. Persist UI preferences (sidebar collapsed, last document and step per application, list filter) through `SettingsRepository`.
- **Prompts:** versioned letter prompts live in `core/application/prompts/`. Extend the mock provider with deterministic letter fixtures so demo mode works end to end.

## 10. Ergonomics and accessibility rules
- Landmarks (`nav`, `main`, `aside`), a skip link, tab order matching visual order, `aria-current` on navigation and steps, slider semantics on the dial, and a live region for generation progress.
- Never rely on color alone; status pills carry an icon and text.
- Every LLM action has a loading state (streaming or skeleton), a Cancel option, and an error state with Retry. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`, and avoid layout shift when switching steps.
- Deletes use undo toasts. Irreversible actions use confirmation dialogs (typed confirmation for wiping all data).
- Persist UI state (sidebar, last step, filters).
- Keep all guarantees from the original brief: WCAG AA contrast, visible focus, full keyboard support.

## 11. Tests
- **Unit:** bullet assembler (including the examples above), contact formatter, letter analysis rules, opener and cliché linter, grounding on letters, Dexie migration, connection-status derivation, banned-terms copy test.
- **Contract:** every exporter passes the contract suite for each kind it supports (PDF text round-trip for a letter, Markdown, Text).
- **Component:** SidebarNav (collapse persistence, `aria-current`), SplitButton, DocumentSwitch, CompactStepper, VoiceControl keyboard, ConfirmDialog with typed confirm.
- **E2E smoke (demo mode):** create application → Job → Build → Review → export; switch to Cover letter → Write → Review → export.
